      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think it\u0027s a good idea to make the backport behave differently from the upstream version.\n\nGiven the intersection of kernel and mainline support timelines, the mainline code will have to support this old behaviour for the better part of a decade. It seems likely that in that time we\u0027ll forget that very old kernels don\u0027t support high values of this sysctl and will try to use them, causing things to break.\n\nIs there a reason you can\u0027t support 16-bit values? The RA lifetime itself is only a 16-bit field anyway, and the hole you\u0027re filling seems to be 2 bytes.",
